{"seq":1237,"lane":"A","class":"commentary-without-new-fact","severity":"minor","evidence":"1237.json, e8: \"You are basically setting yourself up so that if you don't hike in September, people may ask what's going on,\" said Adam Posen, president of the Peterson Institute for International Economics.","rule":"docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html §5.3 and D250: a named analyst's interpretation of an already-recorded event is not kept when it adds no new fact or calculation.","mechanism":"A kept an outside interpretation of the speech alongside the underlying statements, although this passage adds no new fact or calculation."}
{"seq":1238,"lane":"B","class":"wrong-period-filing","severity":"serious","evidence":"1238.json, e4: \"NVIDIA expects its revenue for the next fiscal year to surge by 70%.\" The handover links it to v2, FY2027 revenue; 1244.json identifies the same 70% next-fiscal-year guidance as FY2028 and links it to v72.","rule":"docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html §5.1 and D259: file helpful evidence under the narrowest question it bears on; an open question for the stated period takes precedence.","mechanism":"B linked the forecast to the earlier annual-revenue question despite the existing question for the forecast period. The trace does not establish why B chose v2."}
{"seq":1239,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"reversed-revenue-outcomes","severity":"blocker","evidence":"1239.json, c1: \"Strongly bullish: FY2026 total revenue is below 7011000000 USD\"; \"Strongly bearish: FY2026 total revenue is at least 8118000000 USD.\"","rule":"docs/DECISIONS.md §7 and split_seven_day_poc.py META_SYSTEM: a company outcome runs from strongly bullish to strongly bearish according to what is good or bad for the business.","mechanism":"Record preparation reversed the business meaning of the revenue ranges. The structural ladder checks accepted them, and v78 was written with the reversed labels."}
{"seq":1240,"lane":"B","class":"unrelated-company-filing","severity":"serious","evidence":"1240.json, B e1: \"in Q2 2026 the company paid NT$36 billion in bonuses, representing a 50.6 percent increase compared with Q2 2025 bonuses of NT$24 billion.\" It was filed under v78, ON Semiconductor FY2026 revenue.","rule":"docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html §§5.1 and 5.3 and D250: another company's information needs an identifiable path to the question being answered.","mechanism":"B linked TSMC employee compensation to ON Semiconductor revenue without an evident demand, supply, competition or pricing connection. The trace does not establish why B chose v78."}
{"seq":1240,"lane":"B","class":"unrelated-company-filing","severity":"serious","evidence":"1240.json, B e2: \"Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing generated NT$1.2 trillion in second-quarter revenue, up 36 percent year over year from its Q2 2025 base\" was filed under v78, ON Semiconductor FY2026 revenue.","rule":"docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html §§5.1 and 5.3 and D250: another company's information needs an identifiable path to the question being answered.","mechanism":"B treated TSMC's revenue as evidence for a different company's revenue without establishing a relevant connection."}
{"seq":1240,"lane":"B","class":"unrelated-company-filing","severity":"serious","evidence":"1240.json, B e3: \"Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing's operating profit reached NT$766 billion, with bonuses accounting for 4.7 percent of that operating profit\" was filed under v78, ON Semiconductor FY2026 revenue.","rule":"docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html §§5.1 and 5.3 and D250: another company's information needs an identifiable path to the question being answered.","mechanism":"B linked TSMC's operating profit and compensation ratio to ON Semiconductor revenue without establishing a relevant connection."}
{"seq":1240,"lane":"B","class":"same-fact-two-records","severity":"serious","evidence":"1240.json: A e1 and B e2 both quote \"Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing generated NT$1.2 trillion in second-quarter revenue, up 36 percent year over year\"; _ledger.json writes e4310 under v79 and e4312 under v78.","rule":"D207 and docs/DECISIONS.md §6: daily evidence goes to the narrowest relevant question; D248 distinguishes one statement from multiple records of it.","mechanism":"A and B use the same pre-item library. Their overlapping passages are passed independently to the writer, which stores two records and leaves the B copy under the unrelated question."}
{"seq":1240,"lane":"drop","class":"new-question-evidence-lost","severity":"serious","evidence":"1240.json, B e4: \"a new generation of Apple processors, including the M6 base-tier chip, is planned on TSMC's 2-nanometer process\"; handover: \"no existing question linked\".","rule":"docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html §5.1 and D240: a named customer's relevant action can be helpful evidence without an amount; D209 drops a statement only when no question takes it.","mechanism":"B could link only to questions open before the item, while A opened v79, TSMC FY2026 revenue, from the same article and did not include this customer demand passage. It consequently never reached the new question."}
{"seq":1240,"lane":"judging","class":"growth-applied-twice","severity":"blocker","evidence":"1240.json, v79 judgement: \"Carrying the reported 36% year-over-year growth forward implies about NT$6.53 trillion (NT$4.8T × 1.36).\"","rule":"docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html §7 and D218: distinguish what the source establishes from an inference and support the conclusion.","mechanism":"The judgement annualized a current quarter that already included the reported year-over-year growth, then applied that historical growth again to the current pace without evidence of an equivalent further increase. judging-v7 instructs the model to carry growth forward; the calculation selects the highest outcome."}
{"seq":1242,"lane":"B","class":"missed-customer-evidence","severity":"serious","evidence":"1242.json: \"Xiaomi's recently unveiled Xring O3 processor, developed in partnership with TSMC.\" B returned no evidence; v79, TSMC FY2026 revenue, was already open.","rule":"docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html §5.1 and D240: a named customer's relevant action can be kept without a disclosed amount; D259 permits evidence bearing on demand.","mechanism":"B omitted a recently unveiled customer processor associated with the foundry, so the existing TSMC revenue question did not receive this demand signal. The trace does not establish which instruction caused the omission."}
{"seq":1243,"lane":"B","class":"unsupported-source-attribution","severity":"serious","evidence":"1243.json, B's quote includes \"Nvidia is slated to buy Hugging Face for $12.9 billion\" and a separate CNBC source confirming that acquisition \"has been part of ongoing and recent talks\". The handover keeps only the first sentence while recording original_who as \"an unnamed source cited by CNBC reporters\".","rule":"docs/DECISIONS.md §6 and D218: preserve the original source and do not present an inference as a source fact.","mechanism":"source_quote retained the exact opening passage when the submitted quote ran on across non-contiguous text, but the handover retained B's attribution for the omitted CNBC passage. The stored source attribution therefore connects CNBC's unnamed source to a price that the cited source is not shown to have confirmed."}
{"summary":{"items_read":[1237,1238,1239,1240,1241,1242,1243,1244],"classes":{"commentary-without-new-fact":1,"wrong-period-filing":1,"reversed-revenue-outcomes":1,"unrelated-company-filing":3,"same-fact-two-records":1,"new-question-evidence-lost":1,"growth-applied-twice":1,"missed-customer-evidence":1,"unsupported-source-attribution":1}}}